course: dictionary
lesson: 10771
title: Same letters, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same letters can mean different things, so the context tells you which meaning is right. In «Richmond, VA», VA is in an address, so it is a short form for Virginia, a state in the United States.
explain: In «the VA hospital», the clue is the word hospital, which points to the Department of Veterans Affairs. This is a US group that helps people who served in the armed forces.
explain: Va is also a French word. «Ça va?» is a question meaning "how are you?", and «il va» means "he goes". Before you decide what a word means, check which language and which kind of text you are reading.
fact: VA is short for Virginia in addresses, as in «Richmond, VA».
fact: In the USA, VA can mean the Department of Veterans Affairs, which helps people who served in the armed forces.
fact: In French, «va» means "goes" or "go!", as in «il va» (he goes).
fact: «Ça va?» means "how are you?" or "all right?", and «Ça va bien, merci» means "I'm fine, thanks".
fact: VA can also mean volt-ampere, a unit used on some chargers.
exercise: In the address «Richmond, VA», what does VA stand for? | Vanilla | *Virginia | Valley | Vacation
exercise: «Ça va bien, merci» is French. What does it mean in English? | Where is the station? | Thank you very much | *I'm fine, thanks | Goodbye, see you soon
exercise: In French, «il va à Paris» means "he is going to Paris". What does va mean in this sentence? | has | to | *goes | blue
test: A story about helping soldiers mentions «the VA hospital». What does VA most likely stand for? | *Department of Veterans Affairs | Virginia | Volt-ampere | Very Amazing
test: A French friend writes «Ça va?» on a card. What is the friend asking? | Where do you live? | Can I have a biscuit? | What time is it? | *How are you?
exam: On a charger label you read «VA», and on a French sign you read «Il va à la gare»; which pairing of meanings is correct? | *volt-ampere on the charger, goes on the sign | Virginia on the charger, has on the sign | Very Amazing on the charger, blue on the sign | Victory on the charger, to on the sign
